ed-1:8776 (harm b).\n     5\t\n     6\tBecause the two readers are of two model families, the third read is a panel of two fresh, independent adjudicators, one of each family (a fresh Codex session and a fresh Claude subagent), each given the same case file (`poc/data/citation-probe-2026-11-22/adjudication-case.json`) with the two positions unnamed. A class stands when both adjudicators give it; when they split, the item is unresolved (for Part C, an unresolved difference that would be material if confirmed: the verdict becomes inconclusive). This is stricter than one third reader, chosen so that neither family decides alone.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
